    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "How long does an e-bike battery last?",
        "a": "Watt-hours are volts multiplied by amp-hours. A 36 V, 14 Ah battery is about 504 Wh. Compare watt-hours between bikes, because they relate directly to range."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I leave it charging overnight?",
        "a": "A quality pack often lasts around 500 to 1,000 full charge cycles before capacity drops to roughly 70 to 80 per cent. With normal use that is typically several years."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is a safe way to store a lithium battery?",
        "a": "Charge indoors on a hard surface, away from flammable items, with the charger supplied. Do not charge a damaged battery, and disconnect once it is full."
      },
      {
        "q": "How do I recycle an old battery?",
        "a": "Store it at room temperature and about 40 to 60 per cent charge for long periods. Avoid heat and direct sun, and check it every couple of months."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I fit a bigger battery?",
        "a": "Yes, but it must match the voltage, connector and communication of your bike. Buy from a reputable seller with a warranty, and ask the dealer to confirm compatibility."
      }
    ],
